                <pb facs="0608" n="08 [508]" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg508"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6212/26</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Administrator of the National Recovery
                        Administration</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-23">January 23, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Replying to yours of January
                    12th, I have no suggestions to make about the circular of the League for the
                    Defense of Jewish Rights because regardless of what they may say about the
                    Swastika we are anxious to have people patronize the Blue Eagle.</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hugh S. Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
